WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.167
- It's the first of the month.

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.736
You know what that means:

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:03.503
Rent's due.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:08.041
- [Offscreen voice 1:] Oh, my God! [Laughing]
- [Offscreen voice 2:] Oh, wow.

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:10.577
- [Offscreen voice 3:] Thank you.
I'm so grateful.
- [Offscreen voice 2:] Thank you so much.

00:00:10.577 --> 00:00:11.211
What's up, guys?

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:12.512
I'm Tyrann Mathieu, also

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:13.780
known as The Landlord.

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:14.848
They call me The Landlord

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.616
cuz I own the field, and I take care of

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.818
Chiefs kingdom. But right now my social

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.987
responsibility goes much beyond that.

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:21.988
A lot of people have been

00:00:21.988 --> 00:00:24.524
impacted by COVID-19, especially

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:25.892
in my hometown of New Orleans.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.794
I'm hoping to find a few families

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:29.062
that I can really impact

00:00:29.062 --> 00:00:30.630
and help and love and support.

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:32.098
I'm looking forward to checking them out.

00:00:39.005 --> 00:00:40.707
- My name is Averi Matthews, and

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:42.008
I'm the program coordinator

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:44.544
at the YAYA Arts Center. One of our young

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.113
artists, Quishan Reine, and his family,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:48.915
are an amazing part of our community.

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:50.984
Quishan has been diagnosed

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:53.453
with autism in 2017.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.288
And he has since served as a

00:00:55.288 --> 00:00:56.923
voice for kids with autism.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:58.992
His family has taken on the role as

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:01.127
advocates for youth with autism. His

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:02.896
family volunteers for everything.

00:01:03.063 --> 00:01:04.831
This is an amazing family.

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.233
And any help you could offer them would

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.735
definitely mean the world to them.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:10.503
Thank you so much, Tyrann.

00:01:12.472 --> 00:01:15.875
[Phone ringing]
- Hey, how you doing?

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:17.744
- [Quiana:] Pretty good. How are you?

00:01:17.744 --> 00:01:20.947
- Can you all hear me good?
- [Quiana:] Yes, we can.

00:01:20.947 --> 00:01:22.449
- How's everything going?

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:25.051
- [Quiana:] All right.
- [Quishan:] We're doing good.

00:01:25.051 --> 00:01:26.386
- Taking it easy?

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.054
- [Family:] Yeah.

00:01:28.054 --> 00:01:29.222
- Where is Quishan?

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:31.291
- Oh, I'm right here in the middle.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:33.526
- How you doing, man?
- Oh, I'm doing fine.

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:34.294
How are you doing?

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.063
- Man, I heard a lot of good things about you.

00:01:37.597 --> 00:01:38.331
- Oh, really?

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.700
- Yeah, man. I heard, I heard you can draw.

00:01:41.034 --> 00:01:43.169
I heard you come from a good family, man.

00:01:44.471 --> 00:01:45.839
I heard your spirit is good.

00:01:46.506 --> 00:01:48.608
I heard you kind of like me—you

00:01:48.775 --> 00:01:50.143
like to inspire other people.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:51.478
So I try to, I try to

00:01:51.478 --> 00:01:53.046
do the same thing, man.

00:01:53.046 --> 00:01:56.716
- OK.
That's me.

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:58.451
- I could imagine y'all, you

00:01:58.451 --> 00:02:00.420
guys have been through a lot,

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:03.389
um, you know, since this pandemic.

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:06.359
I heard you guys lost a few family members.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:08.595
- We, first, April 21st, we

00:02:08.595 --> 00:02:10.630
lost the kid's grandmother.
- I'm sorry for that.

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:14.868
- Um, thank you. A few days later, we

00:02:14.868 --> 00:02:17.704
lost an aunt, and I guess maybe a few

00:02:17.704 --> 00:02:19.539
days after that, we lost another aunt.

00:02:19.539 --> 00:02:21.374
So, within the matter of a week,

00:02:21.374 --> 00:02:22.976
we lost three family members.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:26.279
- I'm so sorry that you, that you, that you,

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:28.648
that you all have had to deal with this.

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.184
I truly am. I, I know I can't be with the

00:02:31.184 --> 00:02:33.086
family, but you, but you guys are not alone.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:34.254
I just want to ask you guys,

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:35.522
how is everything going

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.024
financially? Like, how are you guys,

00:02:38.258 --> 00:02:39.292
how are you guys holding up?

00:02:41.861 --> 00:02:43.329
- It was, it was pretty difficult.

00:02:43.363 --> 00:02:44.998
You know, it was pretty difficult.

00:02:45.198 --> 00:02:46.933
My husband, he works two jobs.

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:49.669
So, you know, things were kind of

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:52.505
rough for a moment, but thankfully

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.774
he's gone back to work and we're

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:57.744
kind of seeing a bit of normalcy now.

00:02:58.511 --> 00:03:00.346
- Well, I'm hoping you guys can, can

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:02.682
really continue to lean on each other

00:03:02.682 --> 00:03:05.018
and push each other and encourage each other

00:03:05.351 --> 00:03:07.420
because, you know, you guys are family.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.856
And a lot of times that's all we have.

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.758
Um, but you know my nickname

00:03:11.758 --> 00:03:13.059
is The Landlord, right?
- [Laughing]

00:03:15.061 --> 00:03:17.263
- I run the field. I take

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:17.997
care of the kingdom.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.066
Uh, you know, I heard your story,

00:03:20.066 --> 00:03:22.035
and I just had to reach out.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:25.972
So, I wanted to show some love, but

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.741
I want you to check your texts right now, please.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:30.043
- Oh, my texts? OK.

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:33.713
Oh! He's gonna—they gonna paying 
two months of rent, y'all.

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:38.318
Oh, my goodness. That's awesome. 
Thank you so much.

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:39.986
- Check your account after we hang up,

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.087
and it should be in there for you.

00:03:41.421 --> 00:03:44.524
- That is so awesome. My God. Thank you so much.

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:45.692
- It was a pleasure.

00:03:46.659 --> 00:03:49.262
- Thank you. And we wanted to also tell you

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.998
happy belated birthday.
- Thank you.

00:03:51.998 --> 00:03:53.766
- And—
- Congratulations.

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:56.603
 And congratulations on your Super Bowl win as well.

00:03:56.603 --> 00:03:58.571
- Thank you so much. I appreciate that.

00:03:58.571 --> 00:04:01.140
- And, also too, one small bit: 

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.743
My cousins actually played little league

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:05.878
football with your brother Tyrone.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:08.815
- Ah, that's crazy.
- Yes.

00:04:08.815 --> 00:04:12.585
- You know New Orleans is a small place.
- It is. It is.

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.354
- Quishan, keep it up, man.

00:04:14.354 --> 00:04:15.622
Keep that smile on your face.
- [Quishan:] Mmhmm.

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.624
- Keep being who you are. People

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.491
love who you are, man, so.

00:04:18.491 --> 00:04:20.593
And it was good to meet you.
- [Quishan:] Thank you.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:21.561
- It was good to meet everybody.

00:04:21.861 --> 00:04:25.031
- [Quiana:] Thank you so much.
- [Family:] Thank you.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:28.401
[Everybody saying goodbye]

00:04:28.401 --> 00:04:29.636
- [Quishan:] Thank you very much.

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:32.839
- [Offscreen:] When's football coming back?

00:04:32.839 --> 00:04:36.376
- [Quiana:] We can't wait to see you on the field.

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.410
- Appreciate it. I can't wait to get back out there.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.680
- [Quiana:] I know. Have a good one.

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:41.080
- [Tyrann:] You too.

